Ported (Python to Rust) into crates/kgraf-graph/src/facts.rs, with
significant changes stated here (Apache-2.0 section 4b):
- The bi-temporal model: valid time (valid_at, invalid_at) and transaction
  time (created_at, expired_at) on every fact, stored in SQLite as epoch
  milliseconds.
- The expiry rules: a new fact arriving with invalid_at is expired at once; a
  new fact older than an existing contradicting fact is closed at that fact's
  valid_at; an existing contradicting fact whose interval overlaps and began
  earlier is closed at the new fact's valid_at, expired_at set once.

Changed: Graphiti asks a model which edges contradict or duplicate a new edge.
kGraf decides structurally with no model call: a (subject, predicate) pair
is single-valued, so an open fact with the same subject and predicate and a
different object is a contradiction candidate, and one with the same object is
a duplicate whose episodes gain the new source (the latest 32 are kept, with a
count of all). Nothing is deleted (decision 0028). No embeddings, no graph
database, no LLM-extracted timestamps.

Changed (2026-09-26, review): only open facts are candidates, and an equal
valid_at is a tie broken by transaction time (the later assertion closes the
earlier). Graphiti leaves both open in that case; here at most one fact per
(subject, predicate) is open.
